Subject: [PATCH] logging: expose typed configuration diagnostics without
 changing redaction

Convert all five common/args.cpp LogPrintf producers with original Info levels,
message bytes and branches. Preserve the existing sensitive-value and URL-token
redaction before field capture. ConfigSectionPrefix deliberately stores the old
bracketed display prefix, not a falsely inferred raw section. Existing settings
JSON display strings remain strings; no new settings/redaction behavior.

Add focused full-Logger JSON regressions for all five event branches: double
negation, config sections, sensitive flags, URL tokens, unknown settings and
malformed settings without an error-output vector. Add one owned-node settings
restart functional fixture. Runtime/native checks pending the next coordinated
batch; AST16, inventory fixture, lint13/source341, Ruff and diff checks pass.

Scripted diff (ast-grep-py0.51.0 reviewed mappings):
/private/tmp/lane-n4-build/logging-compose/ast-venv/bin/python contrib/logging/conversion/convert.py --rules contrib/logging/conversion/rules/config-argument-diagnostics.json --report /Users/shammah/repos/lotus-v2-repair-work/logging-cleanup/config-arguments-applied.json --apply
git clang-format --force --binary /opt/homebrew/bin/clang-format --style '{BasedOnStyle: InheritParentConfig, BreakStringLiterals: false}' HEAD -- src/common/args.cpp src/test/logging_event_tests.cpp

Manual native/functional test additions and explicit registry-tail support
